      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a very valid and important concern regarding unconscious bias in leadership selection. It is entirely possible that the preference for traditional networks is unconsciously favoring a specific, homogenous archetype of success. Penalizing high performance solely for a different communication cadence risks stifling innovation and diversity of thought. A truly forward-thinking organization should assess if their culture rewards adaptability, even if it requires adjusting rigid expectations of \"professionalism.\"",
